**Result**: Implemented the AFE-shared L(½+it, χ) evaluation primitive across all χ mod q via the cyclic-DFT identity over (Z/qZ)*. Three implementations cross-verified to 1e-15 relative error.

**Honest measurement**: FFT method gives **bounded constant ~1.7× wall-clock speedup** over OPTIMISED BLAS direct matmul across q ∈ [10², 10⁴]. Theoretical FLOP-ratio (5.8×–22.9×) is real but unrealisable — BLAS hardware FLOP rate (~30 GFLOP/s) vs np.fft Bluestein (~3-5 GFLOP/s) closes most of the algorithmic advantage. **NOT a Correlation-Dichotomy-shaped partial-positive.**

**Methodological correction**: an initial measurement showed 50× speedup that turned out to be Python overhead in slot-1's `all_characters_table()` (φ² double-loop, ~100s at q=10007). Replaced with vectorised `char_table_at_residues()` — 30× speedup, affects all future χ-side experiments.

